WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.070
You've got a streaming cold.

2
00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:06.190
You feel awful, so you ask
the doctor for antibiotics.

3
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.010
The doctor says no.

4
00:00:08.060 --> 00:00:11.150
Yet the same doctor would give
you antibiotics for an infection

5
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.190
caused by bacteria.

6
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.370
Colds are caused by viruses.

7
00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.050
So why are antibiotics
useless against a virus?

8
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.630
In this mission, you'll see
what antibiotics do to bacteria

9
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.890
inside the body.

10
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.510
You'll find out where
viruses do their copying,

11
00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:28.390
and why that matters.

12
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.230
And you'll meet a growing problem:

13
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.510
bacteria that become resistant
when antibiotics are overused.

14
00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:39.930
Your mission: explain why
antibiotics can't cure a cold.
